---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { USER_AGENT } from '../lib/scan';
---

<Base
  title="OGScopeBot: what our crawler does"
  description="OGScopeBot fetches a page only when someone asks for a scan. It reads the head, checks the social image, and stores nothing."
  path="/bot"
>
  <section class="wrap doc">
    <p class="eyebrow">Crawler</p>
    <h1>About OGScopeBot</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      If you found this in your server logs, someone pasted one of your URLs into the checker. We
      fetch a page only when a person asks us to, never on a schedule and never by crawling links.
    </p>

    <h2>How to identify it</h2>
    <div class="snippet"><code>{USER_AGENT}</code></div>

    <h2>What it requests</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>One GET for the page itself, capped at the first 512KB.</li>
      <li>One ranged GET for the image named in your <span class="tag">og:image</span> tag, asking for the first 64KB so we can read its header without downloading the whole file.</li>
      <li>Nothing else. We do not follow links, load scripts, or request other pages.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What it stores</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. The result is built in memory and returned to the person who asked for it. There is no
      database behind the checker and no record of which URLs were scanned.
    </p>

    <h2>Blocking it</h2>
    <p>Add this to your robots.txt and we will stop fetching your pages:</p>
    <div class="snippet"><code>User-agent: OGScopeBot<br />Disallow: /</code></div>
    <p class="note">
      Worth knowing before you do: blocking us does not change anything about how X, Facebook or
      LinkedIn see your site, but it does mean nobody can check your previews with this tool.
    </p>

    <h2>Rate</h2>
    <p>
      One scan is two requests, triggered by one person pressing a button. There is no crawl budget to
      worry about.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc {
    padding: 56px 0 0;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 12px 0 16px;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.4vw, 2.75rem);
  }

  .lede {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  p {
    margin-top: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 9px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .snippet {
    margin-top: 16px;
    background: var(--ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 16px 18px;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .snippet code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: #cfd8e6;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
</style>
